 "notes": [
  "Validated by multiplicity, host undetermined: KIC 6267058 (Gaia 2104058096963805696) 11.79, 16.74 and 29.31 days; KIC 6699887's 47.69-day signal (sibling of the validated KIC 6699887 b).",
  "v1 (multiplicity-v1.json, preserved) let commensurate M/K pairs count as independent when their windows were 80% clear; a 1/k sub-harmonic leaves 1 - 1/k of its windows clear, so v2 judges aliases by S/N, rejects signals sharing two or more events and requires a Hill-stable system. The first v1 run also counted related M/K aliases as independent for two survey signals (preserved as multiplicity-v1-first-run-mk-alias-bug.json). No verdict changed between versions.",
  "KIC 3975580's remaining sibling (BOI-4, shallow, 1.4626 d) is 0.4% from 3:1 and may be an alias; that verdict fails on boosted FPP regardless.",
  "Unresolved low-order ephemeris matches on other stars: 2100041954644727040-1 (7.537 d) vs DR25 TCE KIC 8458662-2 (3.7683 d, 2:1, 12.2 deg); 2106817012155835904 (4.517 d) vs K02199.01 (9.033 d, 1:2, 4.9 deg). Expected chance of a low-order match: 0.14 and 0.15. Pixel-level analysis would be needed.",
  "A survey BOI at the period of a counted M/K sibling is the same signal from the other pipeline and is counted once; the first KIC 6699887 run counted planet b twice and failed the Hill check (preserved as multiplicity-v2-first-run-duplicate-sibling-bug.json).",
  "v3 adds Rowe et al. 2014 section 5.9 exactly: fitted-model S/N (not the search S/N) > 10, > 15 below 4 days; period above 1.6 days; not V-shaped. No verdict changed."
 ],
 "scope": "Every completed non-validated V3 campaign with FPP < 50% and NFPP < 0.1%, plus the KIC 6267058 system. A failed condition is a negative result; the candidates keep their TRICERATOPS+ categories."
}